    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line in `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` already logged `membershipLevel` but was missing `membershipNumber`. I added it while keeping every existing field:\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}\",\n        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),\n        org.springframework.samples.petclinic.util.MembershipLevels.levelFor(owner),\n        owner.getMembershipNumber());\n```\n\n`membershipNumber` is assigned by the `membershipNumber` step (`AssignMembershipNumber`) earlier in the `owners.POST` pipeline, so it's populated by the time the `respond` step logs it \u2014 confirmed by the emitted line:\n\n```\nAUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-11 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```\n\nTest suite: **BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes).",
